the knowledge base prescriptiverule includes:

the text of the source description is at "sources/PrescriptiveRule.ttl".

% Who bears a duty: the agent of this role of the action (lomo.le).
the bearer role is addresser.


requirement art 4 par 1 is identified by "http://example.org/Requirement_Art4_Par1".

requirement art 4 par 1 is a prescriptive rule.

requirement art 4 par 1 has the modality obligation.

requirement art 4 par 1 has the requirement type "http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/administrative-obligation/c_80214a02".

requirement art 4 par 1 produces action art 4 data collection.

requirement art 4 par 1 produces action art 4 data transmission.

requirement art 4 par 1 has the legal text "The detailed topics, transmission frequencies, reference periods and the dimensions related to sensitive species, organic production and regional breakdown on fisheries and aquaculture statistics referred to in Article 1, shall be as set out in the Annex.".

requirement art 4 par 1 is established in "https://data.europa.eu/eli/dl/proc/2025/96/cod/doc/com/COM_2025_425/FINAL/eng/art_4/par_1".


requirement art 30 par 1 publication obligation is identified by "http://example.org/Requirement_Art30_Par1_PublicationObligation".

requirement art 30 par 1 publication obligation is a prescriptive rule.

requirement art 30 par 1 publication obligation has the modality obligation.

requirement art 30 par 1 publication obligation has the requirement type "http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/administrative-obligation/c_80214a02".

requirement art 30 par 1 publication obligation produces action art 30 publish.

requirement art 30 par 1 publication obligation has the legal text "Member States shall ensure that undertakings publish within a reasonable period of time, which shall not exceed 12 months after the balance sheet date, the duly approved annual financial statements and the management report, together with the opinion submitted by the statutory auditor or audit firm.".

requirement art 30 par 1 publication obligation is established in "http://data.europa.eu/eli/dir/2013/34/oj/art_30/par_1".


requirement art 10 par 2 is identified by "http://example.org/Requirement_Art10_Par2".

requirement art 10 par 2 is a prescriptive rule.

requirement art 10 par 2 has the modality obligation.

requirement art 10 par 2 has the requirement type "http://publications.europa.eu/resource/dataset/administrative-obligation/c_39b9f824".

requirement art 10 par 2 has the legal text "Until [date of entry into force + 4 years] the competent authorities shall require the submission of only Part I of the physical registration certificate when re-registering a vehicle previously registered in another Member State. Until that date, they may also accept the presentation of a mobile registration certificate, if any.".

requirement art 10 par 2 is established in "https://data.europa.eu/eli/dl/proc/2025/96/cod/doc/com/COM_2025_179/FINAL/art_10/par_2".


